# Products the build installs INSIDE a build/usrtrees root.
#
# usrtrees names the directories that are shape -- the tree as the tapes have
# it -- and ipnxbuild calls every file that appears in them during a build
# derived, for ipnxclean to sweep.  That is right for an object file and wrong
# for an installed program's own data, which a package puts where the program
# looks, whatever usrtrees says about the directory.  A product swept is a
# program broken in a way no build reports: the install succeeds, the clean
# succeeds, and the program fails the first time somebody runs it.
#
# Each row is one such product.  ipnxclean keeps it, ipnxbuild's overwrite
# report expects the build to rewrite it, and tools/v10-tree-check.py expects
# it on the disk and not in git.  ONE LIST FOR ALL THREE: maps/map used to be
# written into each of them by hand, and the second product was missed by all
# three.  One path per row, /usr-relative; anything after it is a note.
maps/map		map's mkfile installs the program here; map.sh's MAPPROG and every man page agree
local/lib/flex.skel	flex compiles in /usr/local/lib/flex.skel (flex/Makefile:21-23); swept by every build until 8 Oct 2026
